# Copy to web/.env.local and fill both values.
#
# Both of these are PUBLIC. Anything prefixed with VITE_ is inlined into the
# JavaScript bundle at build time and is readable by anyone who loads the page.
# That is fine for these two: the project URL is public, and the anon key is a
# project identifier that grants no access on its own - row access is decided
# by Supabase RLS after a user signs in.
#
# NEVER put SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY here, or any other server-only secret.
# It bypasses RLS entirely and lives only in GitHub Actions secrets.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SERVER-side variables, used only by the functions in web/api/. None of them
# has a VITE_ prefix, so Vite cannot inline them and the browser can never
# read them. vite.config.ts does not set `envPrefix`, which is what keeps
# Vite's VITE_-only default in force - do not add one.
#
#   GITHUB_DISPATCH_TOKEN   fine-grained PAT, Stacheydev/NBLG only,
#                           Actions: Read and write
#   SUPABASE_URL            same value as VITE_SUPABASE_URL above
#   SUPABASE_ANON_KEY       same value as VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY above
#   GROQ_API_KEY            Groq inference key, for the Analyze Lead endpoint
#
# The Vercel dashboard (Project Settings -> Environment Variables) is the
# source of truth for all four. Never hand-write a real credential into this
# file or into .env.local.
#
# To run the web/api/ functions locally you need `vercel dev` - plain
# `vite dev` serves the frontend only and never executes them. Get the values
# with `vercel env pull web/.env.local`, which writes the real ones into the
# gitignored .env.local for you. That is the only sanctioned way a credential
# reaches .env.local: pulled from Vercel, never typed in by hand.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
